+## 🎯 Project Overview
+
+Pulseboard is a small web product for team facilitators who lose follow-up actions after weekly meetings. A facilitator uploads a meeting transcript, reviews the proposed action items it yields, and must confirm an owner and due date before an item can become eligible for a reminder. The pilot matters because five teams need a lightweight way to turn meeting discussion into accountable follow-through without adopting a meeting recorder, replacing their calendar, or allowing an autonomous system to message people.
+
+## 🎨 Project Type & Scale
+
+**Type**: Web Application (browser-based, responsive)
+
+**Estimated Scale**: Level 2 — a moderate, pilot-sized feature set covering transcript intake, review, action accountability, and a deliberately gated reminder capability for five teams.
+
+**Primary Domain**: Enterprise/B2B — team meeting follow-through and action accountability.
+
+**Domain Expertise Required**: No specialist domain is evidenced at specification time. The product uses ordinary team-workflow concepts; any privacy, retention, or workplace-policy requirements become explicit context work once the pilot environment is known.
+
+## 🚀 Vision & Goals
+
+### Vision Statement
+
+A world where team facilitators can turn weekly meeting discussion into owned, time-bound follow-through so that important actions do not disappear after the meeting ends.
+
+### Primary Goals
+
+1. **Review adoption**: Have facilitators review at least 80% of proposed action items during the four-week pilot.
+   - Success looks like: proposed items are actively accepted, edited, or rejected rather than accumulating unreviewed.
+   - Key metric: reviewed proposed items ÷ all proposed items.
+
+2. **Accountability improvement**: Reduce unowned overdue actions by 30% after four weeks.
+   - Success looks like: fewer overdue actions exist without a clearly confirmed owner.
+   - Key metric: count of overdue actions without an owner, compared with the pilot baseline.
+
+3. **Safe follow-through**: Ensure no reminder is scheduled unless a facilitator has explicitly confirmed both an owner and due date.
+   - Success looks like: every reminder-eligible item has a recorded facilitator confirmation, owner, and due date.
+   - Key metric: number of scheduled reminders lacking any required confirmation field; target: zero.
+
